IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Dates the Federal-State Extended Unemployment Compensation Act of 1970 states, and the small
-- arithmetic its rules share. Every date is defined once, here, and named by the calendar date;
-- the other euca- modules use these names and never repeat a figure.
-- `Date day month year` is little-endian; each definition carries the ISO date in a comment.
-- The stable l4 has no YMD, and DATE values compare directly with AT LEAST and AT MOST.

§ `Dates the Act states, and arithmetic its rules share`

§§ `Dates in the Act's own words`

-- The date of enactment is not stated in the Act's operative words. It appears in the OLRC's
-- title block (line 19) and, in square brackets, in s 207(b)(1). Both are editorial matter
-- printed by the OLRC; the fork register records that the figure is carried from there.
-- src:19 | Aug. 10, 1970, 84 Stat. 708
-- src:140 | not earlier than 60 days after the date of the enactment of this Act [Aug. 10, 1970]
@ref date of enactment of title II of Pub. L. 91-373, Aug. 10, 1970 (src:19 src:140)
GIVETH A DATE
`the date this title was enacted` MEANS Date 10 8 1970 -- 1970-08-10

-- s 207(b)(1): "not earlier than 60 days after the date of the enactment of this Act".
-- src:140 | not earlier than 60 days after the date of the enactment of this Act
@ref s 207(b)(1) (src:140)
GIVETH A DATE
`60 days after the date this title was enacted` MEANS `the date this title was enacted` PLUS 60 -- 1970-10-09

-- src:89 | Effective with respect to compensation for weeks of unemployment beginning after March 30, 1977 (or, if later, the date established pursuant to State law)
@ref s 203(d), closing paragraph, first sentence (src:89)
GIVETH A DATE
`30 March 1977` MEANS Date 30 3 1977 -- 1977-03-30

-- src:55 | Paragraphs (3) and (4) shall not apply to weeks of unemployment beginning after March 6, 1993, and before January 1, 1995
-- src:94 | Effective with respect to compensation for weeks of unemployment beginning after March 6, 1993
@ref s 202(a)(7) and s 203(f)(1) (src:55 src:94)
GIVETH A DATE
`6 March 1993` MEANS Date 6 3 1993 -- 1993-03-06

-- src:55 | Paragraphs (3) and (4) shall not apply to weeks of unemployment beginning after March 6, 1993, and before January 1, 1995
@ref s 202(a)(7) (src:55)
GIVETH A DATE
`1 January 1995` MEANS Date 1 1 1995 -- 1995-01-01

-- The Act says "the date of enactment of the Tax Relief, Unemployment Insurance Reauthorization,
-- and Job Creation Act of 2010"; the figure is the OLRC's bracketed note.
-- src:89 | after the date of enactment of the Tax Relief, Unemployment Insurance Reauthorization, and Job Creation Act of 2010 [Dec. 17, 2010]
-- src:100 | after the date of enactment of the Tax Relief, Unemployment Insurance Reauthorization, and Job Creation Act of 2010 [Dec. 17, 2010]
@ref s 203(d), closing paragraph, second sentence, and s 203(f)(2) (src:89 src:100)
GIVETH A DATE
`17 December 2010` MEANS Date 17 12 2010 -- 2010-12-17

-- src:89 | and ending on or before December 31, 2013
-- src:100 | and ending on or before December 31, 2013
@ref s 203(d), closing paragraph, second sentence, and s 203(f)(2) (src:89 src:100)
GIVETH A DATE
`31 December 2013` MEANS Date 31 12 2013 -- 2013-12-31

-- src:137 | in applying section 203, no extended benefit period may begin with a week beginning before January 1, 1972
-- src:140 | which begins earlier than January 1, 1972
@ref s 207(a)(1) and s 207(b)(1) (src:137 src:140)
GIVETH A DATE
`1 January 1972` MEANS Date 1 1 1972 -- 1972-01-01

-- src:138 | section 204 shall apply only with respect to weeks of unemployment beginning after December 31, 1971
@ref s 207(a)(2) (src:138)
GIVETH A DATE
`31 December 1971` MEANS Date 31 12 1971 -- 1971-12-31

-- src:144 | with respect to any week of unemployment which begins prior to July 1, 1972
@ref s 207(c)(1) (src:144)
GIVETH A DATE
`1 July 1972` MEANS Date 1 7 1972 -- 1972-07-01

-- s 208(a)(1): "the date of enactment of this section"; the figure is the OLRC's bracketed note.
-- src:148 | for any weeks of unemployment beginning after the date of enactment of this section [Feb. 22, 2012]
@ref s 208(a)(1) (src:148)
GIVETH A DATE
`22 February 2012` MEANS Date 22 2 2012 -- 2012-02-22

§§ `Arithmetic the rules share (not provisions of the Act)`

-- A week is carried as the DATE on which it begins, so "the third week after" is 21 days on.
GIVEN week IS A DATE
      weeks IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the week that falls this many weeks after` week weeks MEANS week PLUS (7 TIMES weeks)

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of two amounts` a b MEANS
    IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of two amounts` a b MEANS
    IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smallest of three amounts` a b c MEANS
    `the lesser of two amounts` a (`the lesser of two amounts` b c)

GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of two dates` a b MEANS
    IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earlier of two dates` a b MEANS
    IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b
